  <model metaid="meta_spt_liver_cell" id="spt_liver_cell" name="Model for hepatic S -&gt; P + T metabolism in the liver" substanceUnits="mmole" timeUnits="min" volumeUnits="litre" areaUnits="m2" lengthUnits="metre" extentUnits="mmole">
    <notes>
      <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <p>Model for hepatic metabolism of substrate (S) to product (P) and toxic byproduct (T)
encoded in <a href="http://sbml.org">SBML</a> format.</p>
        <p>The model consists of of a single liver compartment with single metabolic conversion
reaction which converts the substrate S to the product P and a toxic byproduct T <code>S -&gt; P + T</code>.
The product P can be exported from the liver with the toxic side product T being confined to
the liver.</p>
        <p>If the hepatic concentration of the toxic substance T reaches a critical threshold necrosis is
initiated. The necrosis is smooth and irreversible and stops the rates of the cell.</p>
        <p>
          <strong>version:</strong> 0.10.0</p>
          <h2>Changelog</h2>
          <p>
            <strong>version 0.10.0</strong>
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>pattern 7 is the protein set from outside, <code>protein = protein_ext</code>, so that
a simulator can feed in the protein per cell (e.g. the CYP2E1 amount measured
on a slide)</li>
            <li>the cell variant <code>spt_liver_cell</code> has the elements of the liver model
without the <code>comp</code> and <code>distrib</code> packages: no ports, and the constant
<code>protein_random</code> = 0.5 instead of the random initial assignment</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            <strong>version 0.9.0</strong>
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>pattern 6 is the measured CYP2E1 zonation profile of the mouse liver, the
mean profile of three control mice, and no longer the piecewise linear
interpolation of twelve digitized bins. How the pattern was formed:
<ul>
              <li>measured: the brown of the CYP2E1 immunostaining of three whole
sections, read every 1.8 µm against the clear glass and set against its
500 µm surroundings (palest tenth 0, darkest tenth 1); the lobules are
the watershed of the blurred brown (604 lobules), the position is
<code>p = dp/(dp + dc)</code> of Albadry et al. 2024 with the distances to the
nearest portal and central point; one curve per mouse from 0 at its
portal end to 1 at its top, the three averaged
(<code>data/mouse_cyp2e1_profile.csv</code>, the forty positions of the pattern
scan)</li>
              <li>fitted: the Hill rise of pattern 2 minus its periportal value, so the
protein is 0 at the periportal pole, with the measured <code>K</code> = 0.5847 and
<code>n</code> = 1.954 (half of the rise at <code>position</code> 0.55, pattern 2 is almost a
step at 0.75); the fitted equation is off the measured mean by 0.013
(root mean square) and at most 0.024 on the 0 to 1 scale of the
measurement, 0.015 and 0.029 as the pattern is normalized</li>
              <li>normalized: the profile is divided by its perivenous value
<code>1/(1 + K^n)</code> = 0.7405, so that the pattern runs from 0 at the
periportal to 1 at the perivenous pole, as the other patterns of a
profile do</li>
            </ul></li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            <strong>version 0.8.0</strong>
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>the zonation patterns are normalized to a maximum of 1 instead of the protein
content of the lobulus geometry: the random pattern draws in [0, 1], the
linear and sharp patterns are unscaled, the CYP2E1 pattern is divided by the
largest of its medians, the constant pattern is 0.5</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            <strong>version 0.7.0</strong>
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>experimental CYP2E1 zonation pattern of the mouse liver (pattern 6)</li>
            <li>the scaling factors of the patterns are computed on the geometry of the
lobulus, the factors of the patterns 1-4 change by 1.1% to 4.5%</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            <strong>version 0.6.0</strong>
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>inflows and outflows for model coupling added</li>
            <li>necrosis is smooth and irreversible, the dead fraction of the cells in [0, 1]</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            <strong>version 0.5.4</strong>
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>typo fix: <code>TDETOX_Km_napqi</code> -&gt; <code>TDETOX_Km_T</code></li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            <strong>version 0.5.3</strong>
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>fixed switching thresholds for C++ export</li>
            <li>additional annotations and documentation</li>
            <li>removed source reactions</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            <strong>version 0.5</strong>
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>updated gamma thresholds</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            <strong>version 0.1</strong>
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>initial model version based on minimal apap model</li>
          </ul>
          <p>The content of this model has been carefully created in a manual research effort.</p>
